  "narrative": "Synthesis report. The due deadlines are resolved clearly. H53, the main positive feature_002 claim, is accepted and closed: discovery was +0.810 (95% interval +0.745 to +0.875) and independent validation was +0.803 with a stringent interval +0.706 to +0.900. The full validation interval remains far above the 0.15-unit threshold, so within this dataset the association is large, precise, and reproducible. This is stronger than a marginal discovery alone and, together with validated H55, argues that feature_002 is not merely a proxy for feature_010. H74, the decisive residual negative feature_037 claim within feature_010=0 and feature_002=0, is also accepted and closed: discovery +0.814 and validation +0.845, validation interval +0.770 to +0.921. Under the negative-direction signed convention, a positive signed estimate corresponds to a raw exposed-minus-comparator decrease, so feature_037=1 is associated with approximately a 0.845-unit lower composite dependency score in a stratum designed to remove the two positive tags. This validates separable measured negative association for feature_037 in this dataset, though it still does not establish causal independence or external generalizability. H5, the negative feature_058 main-effect claim, remains rejected and closed. Discovery was essentially null and validation was signed +0.0156 with interval -0.0689 to +0.1000; the independent interval includes zero and the point estimate is far below the claimed-magnitude threshold. Overall supported dataset-specific pattern: feature_010=1 is strongly positive, feature_002=1 is strongly positive and independently validated, and feature_037=1 is strongly negative with validated conditional residual support. The negative screen for feature_058 is resolved as non-meaningful. The main unresolved area is feature_063. H80, the reversed negative feature_063 claim, has signed estimate +0.2386 and interval +0.1454 to +0.3318. The point estimate exceeds the 0.15 threshold, but the lower bound falls slightly below it, so the evidence is suggestive rather than decisive. I keep H80 unresolved and active. The next most informative analysis is residual testing of feature_063: existing H81 and H82 plus two newly registered conditional feature_063 claims, one within feature_037=1 and one within feature_010=0, feature_002=0, and feature_037=0. These will test whether the negative feature_063 association persists when strong core tags are absent or held fixed. If the residuals are large and robust, validation of H80 would be the most informative follow-up; if they attenuate, feature_063 is more likely a correlated proxy or marker of the existing structure. The pending feature_010 and feature_002 interactions with feature_037=1, H68 and H69, remain relevant for effect modification but are secondary to resolving feature_063. All conclusions are descriptive associations in the supplied dataset, not causal effects or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Validated dataset-specific core: feature_010=1 positive; feature_002=1 positive and validated; feature_037=1 negative and H74 residual validated. H5 negative feature_058 main effect is confirmed null/rejected. H80 negative feature_063 is borderline unresolved: point 0.239, lower 0.145. Next analyze feature_063 residuals (H81/H82 plus new feature_037=1 and triple-absent claims) and interactions H68/H69. If feature_063 residuals persist, request validation of H80; if attenuate, treat as correlated proxy. All findings are descriptive and dataset-specific, not causal or generalizable."
